ion + solvency rules. (Spark Docs) Meets criteria: creates credit and enforces liquidation/solvency fully onchain; interest and risk logic are protocol-defined per market. (docs.morpho.org)": "Meets criteria: issues credit from smart-contract pools; loan terms are programmatic; default processes can trigger onchain liquidation pathways (delegate-triggered). (GitHub)", "Systemic Risk Exposure High (systemically important liquidity + collateral hub) High (core, long-lived DeFi credit primitive with broad integrations) Very High (DAI is systemically embedded across DeFi and beyond) High (meaningful stablecoin and ETH market integration within Sky ecosystem) (Blockworks) High (rapidly becoming core lending primitive; systemic exposure rises with integration density)": "High (large onchain credit venue; integration density increasing)", "Upstream Dependencies DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; oracle networks; stablecoin liquidity; governance/risk stewards Oracles (Chainlink); DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; stablecoin liquidity Oracles; keeper/liquidation infrastructure; governance processes; real-world legal structures (for RWAs) Oracles; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; Sky/Maker liquidity inputs; governance operations (Blockworks) Oracles; liquidator/keeper ecosystem; market curation/allocators; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution": "Underwriting + pool delegate operations; collateral custody/monitoring; smart contract risk management (Maple Governance Forum)"}, "source_label": "Lending Markets"}'::jsonb),
  ('truefi', 'TrueFi', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'lending-markets', 'https://truefi.io (TrueFi)', ARRAY['Borrower-specific smart contracts (e.g.', 'AutomatedLineOfCredit) manage borrowing', 'repayment', 'borrower is sole borrower on that contract (TrueFi Docs)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Credit protocol offering onchain lending via pools and borrower-specific Lines of Credit, with programmatic repayment flows and default backstops. (TrueFi Docs)", "extras": {"Collateral Types Supported ERC-20s; ETH; widely supports LST collateral in certain markets (risk-parameter dependent) ERC-20s; ETH (wrapped); selected stablecoins; LST support market-dependent (primarily via governance-approved assets) ETH; ERC-20s; selected LSTs; RWAs (via specialized vaults) ERC-20s + ETH (incl. stETH, DAI, sDAI at launch; asset set is governance/risk-managed) (TradingView) ERC-20s; market-defined collateral/loan pairs (including LSTs, stablecoins, and other ERC-20 collateral depending on market config) (docs.morpho.org)": "Primarily stablecoin credit; borrower-specific lines of credit; collateralization varies by product", "Dependency Concentration Risk High oracle reliance + large-collateral concentration risk (market-dependent); governance/parameter-change latency risk High oracle reliance; Medium–High asset concentration risk in v3 base asset; governance latency risk High oracle reliance; High governance concentration risk; Medium–High RWA dependency risk High oracle reliance + governance/parameter-change latency risk; asset concentration risk (DAI-centric design) (Spark Docs) High oracle dependence (per-market); configuration/parameter risk; integration/curation risk (markets can be permissionlessly created but quality varies) (mixbytes.io)": "High borrower/manager concentration risk; Medium–High governance/operations risk; reliance on backstop sizing and correct liquidation triggers (TrueFi Docs)", "Downstream Consumers Yield strategies, leveraged LPs, hedged carry, structured products, derivatives margin users Yield strategies, leveraged positions, DAO treasuries, arbitrage and carry strategies DEX liquidity, lending protocols, yield strategies, derivatives, DAOs, payment rails Yield strategies, stablecoin allocators, leverage users, structured products integrating DAI liquidity Vaults/allocators, structured lending products, leveraged strategies, institutional deployers using Morpho rails": "Yield allocators, credit strategies, structured credit products", "Governance Model Token governance (AAVE) via Aave DAO processes; proposals/voting for parameter changes (aave.com) Token governance (COMP) via Compound DAO proposals and voting Token governance (MKR) with executive votes and onchain spell execution Governance via SPK token; Snapshot/signaling and governance system documented by Spark (Spark Docs) Token governance via MORPHO; weighted voting and defined governance powers (docs.morpho.org)": "TRU token staking aligns risk managers; governance via DAO processes reflected in docs and forum practice (TrueFi Docs)", "Historical Stress Events Yes (v1 largely frozen/disabled for new supply/borrow; legacy positions remain manageable) (messari.io) Yes (v2 experienced stress events and governance interventions; migration to v3 reflects risk simplification lessons) Yes (notably March 2020 “Black Thursday” auction failures; subsequent mechanism redesigns) No major protocol-loss event cited in core docs; treat as “monitor” (bug bounty active) (Immunefi) Yes (documented oracle-manipulation event on a specific market; plus a frontend-related incident where contracts unaffected) (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Yes (publicly reported defaults and notices of default) (CoinDesk)", "Interest Rate Model Utilization-based variable rates; also supports “stable” borrow rate mode (market-specific) Utilization-based interest rate curves per asset (v2); simplified rate model with base/borrow asset separation (v3) Governance-set stability fees per vault