ncy during fast markets. Also track version/market fragmentation (v1 frozen vs v3 active) when analyzing risk. (messari.io) Research focus: differences between v2 and v3 risk profiles; base-asset concentration in v3; liquidation throughput under stress; governance response speed during incidents. Research focus: auction efficiency during stress, oracle latency, RWA exposure and offchain enforcement risk, governance concentration, and emergency shutdown assumptions. Watchpoints: Aave v3 fork deltas (custom DAI/sDAI logic), oracle stack and feed coverage, asset-list governance, and liquidation throughput under stablecoin stress. Also note Spark’s bug bounty posture. (Spark Docs) Watchpoints: oracle selection/config is a first-order risk surface (market-by-market). Validate LLTV choice, oracle robustness, and liquidation liquidity for collateral. Review post-mortems for oracle manipulation and operational incidents. (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Watchpoints: whitelisting/credit governance, liquidation reliability for protocol collateral, upgrade/admin controls, and liquidity constraints (ability for suppliers to exit). (Alpha Venture)", "Primary Role in DeFi Base credit + leverage layer for Ethereum DeFi Base credit layer and leverage primitive for Ethereum DeFi Stablecoin issuance + base credit layer for DeFi DAI-centered credit & liquidity venue; major stablecoin + ETH collateral borrowing/supply rails inside Sky ecosystem (Blockworks) Base lending primitive for permissionless risk markets; “lending infrastructure” others build vaults/allocators on top of": "Protocol-to-protocol liquidity backstop / capital-efficiency rail (B2B lending) (Medium)", "Protocol Status Active (v3 widely used; v1 largely frozen) (messari.io) Active (v3 “Comet” is primary; v2 largely deprecated/frozen for growth) Active (DAI issuance core to Ethereum DeFi) Active Active": "Active, but with notable operational/liquidity constraints communicated by the project app (app.ib.xyz)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending; collateralized credit issuance; onchain interest rate mechanics; liquidation + solvency enforced by protocol logic. (aave.com) Meets criteria: issues credit onchain against collateral; defines interest rates, liquidation logic, and solvency rules fully in smart contracts. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing; collateralized credit issuance; explicit liquidation and solvency logic; interest (stability fees) set and enforced onchain. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending, collateralized credit issuance, onchain interest + liquidation + solvency rules. (Spark Docs) Meets criteria: creates credit and enforces liquidation/solvency fully onchain; interest and risk logic are protocol-defined per market. (docs.morpho.org)": "Meets criteria: onchain lending/borrowing, programmatic credit issuance, and protocol-defined solvency + liquidation rules (plus whitelisted credit lines). (Messari)", "Systemic Risk Exposure High (systemically important liquidity + collateral hub) High (core, long-lived DeFi credit primitive with broad integrations) Very High (DAI is systemically embedded across DeFi and beyond) High (meaningful stablecoin and ETH market integration within Sky ecosystem) (Blockworks) High (rapidly becoming core lending primitive; systemic exposure rises with integration density)": "Medium–High (less embedded than Aave/Compound; higher tail risk due to whitelisted undercollateralized design) (defillama.com)", "Upstream Dependencies DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; oracle networks; stablecoin liquidity; governance/risk stewards Oracles (Chainlink); DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; stablecoin liquidity Oracles; keeper/liquidation infrastructure; governance processes; real-world legal structures (for RWAs) Oracles; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; Sky/Maker liquidity inputs; governance operations (Blockworks) Oracles; liquidator/keeper ecosystem; market curation/allocators; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution": "Oracles; liquidation bots; governance/upgrade ops; integrations with other protocols that may be whitelisted borrowers (Messari)"}, "source_label": "Lending Markets"}'::jsonb),
  ('reflexer-rai', 'Reflexer (RAI)', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'lending-markets', 'https://reflexer.finance (Reflexer)', ARRAY['Over-collateralized borrowing: users lock ETH in SAFEs and mint RAI against it', 'protocol enforces debt ceilings and collateralization constraints (Reflexer)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Ethereum protocol where users mint RAI, a non-pegged, ETH-backed stable asset, via SAFE positions; solvency and liquidations are enforced onchain with auctions. (Reflexer)", "extras": {"Collateral Types Supported ERC-20s; ETH; widely supports LST collateral in certain markets (risk-parameter dependent) ERC-20s; ETH (wrapped); selected stablecoins; LST support market-dependent (primarily via governance-approved assets) ETH; ERC-20s; selected LSTs; RWAs (via specialized vaults) ERC-20s + ETH (incl. stETH, DAI, sDAI at launch; asset set is governance/risk-managed) (TradingView) ERC-20s; market-defined collateral/loan pairs (including LSTs, stablecoins, and other ERC-20 collateral depending on market config) (docs.morpho.org)": "ETH collateral (RAI is ETH-backed; SAFE positions mint RAI) (Reflexer)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High oracle reliance + large-collateral concentration risk (market-dependent); governance/parameter-change latency risk High oracle reliance; Medium–High asset concentration risk in v3 base asset; governance latency risk High oracle reliance; High governance concentration risk; Medium–High RWA dependency risk High oracle reliance + governance/parameter-change latency risk; asset concentration risk (DAI-centric design) (Spark Docs) High oracle dependence (per-market); configuration/parameter risk; integration/curation risk (markets can be permissionlessly created but quality varies) (mixbytes.io)": "High ETH-only collateral concentration; High oracle/relayer dependency; Medium auction/keeper participation risk (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Downstream Consumers Yield strategies, leveraged LPs, hedged carry, structured products, derivatives margin users Yield strategies, leveraged positions, DAO treasuries, arbitrage and carry strategies DEX liquidity, lending protocols, yield strategies, derivatives, DAOs, payment rails Yield strategies, stablecoin allocators, leverage users, structured products integrating DAI liquidity Vaults/allocators, structured lending products, leveraged strategies, institutional deployers using Morpho rails": "Stablecoin strategies, structured products, collateral use cases, DeFi participants seeking non-USD-pegged stability mechanisms (Reflexer)", "Governance Model Token governance (AAVE) via Aave DAO processes; proposals/voting for parameter changes (aave.com) Token governance (COMP) via Compound DAO proposals and voting Token governance (MKR) with executive votes and onchain spell execution Governance via SPK token; Snapshot/signaling and governance system documented by Spark (Spark Docs) Token governance via MORPHO; weighted voting and defined governance powers (docs.morpho.org)": "FLX “ungovernance” model: token holders can remove remaining governance surfaces over time (goal: minimize governance) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Historical Stress Events Yes (v1 largely frozen/disabled for new supply/borrow; legacy positions remain manageable) (messari.io) Yes (v2 experienced stress events and governance interventions; migration to v3 reflects risk simplification lessons) Yes (notably March 2020 “Black Thursday” auction failures; subsequent mechanism redesigns) No major protocol-loss event cited in core docs; treat as “monitor” (bug bounty active) (Immunefi) Yes (documented oracle-manipulation event on a specific market; plus a frontend-related incident where contracts unaffected) (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Monitor (stress expresses via auction performance + redemption-rate dynamics rather than classic money-market runs) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Interest Rate Model Utilization-based variable rates; also supports “stable” borrow rate mode (market-specific) Utilization-based interest rate curves per asset (v2); simplified rate model with base/borrow asset separation (v3) Governance-set stability fees per vault type (effectively interest rates) Utilization-based IR model (Aave v3 lineage) + custom DAI/sDAI strategies in Spark context (Medium) Market-selected Interest Rate Models (IRMs); IRMs/LLTVs are constrained by governance whitelists (docs.morpho.org)": "Redemption Rate / Redemption Price mechanism (control-theory/PID-style policy) drives target price dynamics; not a utilization-based money market rate (Reflexer)", "Isolation of Risk Risk primarily at market/reserve parameter level (not isolated per-user); isolation features exist in newer versions/markets but not “isolated pools” by default Moderate isolation: v3 introduces asset isolation via a single base asset with segmented collateral; v2 uses shared pools High isolation at vault-type level; each collateral type has independent parameters Shared pool risk by asset/reserve parameters (not per-market isolation like Morpho Blue) High isolation: each market is isolated and immutable by design (docs.morpho.org)": "System-level shared risk (single collateral type, shared liquidation + auction plumbing), rather than isolated pools (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Launch Year 2020 (v1 Ethereum mainnet) (aave.com) 2018 (v2 on Ethereum) 2017 (Single-Collateral DAI; Multi-Collateral DAI in 2019) 2023 (public launch May 9, 2023) (X (formerly Twitter)) 2023 (Morpho Blue introduced Oct 2023) (morpho.org)": "2021-02-17 (RAI mainnet launch) (Medium)", "Lending Model Pooled liquidity markets (multi-asset) Pooled liquidity markets (v2); single-collateral base with isolated borrow assets (v3/Comet) CDP / Vault-based collateralized lending Pooled liquidity markets (Aave v3-derived money market) (Spark Docs) Permissionless, isolated lending markets (1 collateral + 1 loan asset per market) (docs.morpho.org)": "CDP / SAFE-based borrowing (Maker-style architecture via GEB framework) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Liquidation Mechanism Onchain liquidations triggered when Health Factor < 1; liquidators repay debt for collateral + bonus (bonus/thresholds per asset, governance/risk-managed) (aave.com) Onchain liquidations when collateral value breaches borrow limits; liquidators repay debt for collateral at protocol-defined incentives Onchain liquidation via auctions (debt, collateral, surplus); keeper participation required Health Factor-based liquidations (HF < 1), onchain seizure/repay mechanics (Spark Docs) Standard liquidation when LTV exceeds LLTV; liquidators repay debt and seize collateral at discount (protocol-enforced) (docs.morpho.org)": "LiquidationEngine → CollateralAuctionHouse: unsafe SAFEs can be liquidated and collateral is auctioned to cover debt; keepers participate in auctions (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Maintaining Organization Aave DAO (governance) + Aave Labs (major dev & interface/operator tooling) (aave.com) Compound DAO (governance) with historical development by Compound Labs MakerDAO (DAO-governed protocol) with core units / contributors maintaining modules Spark Governance (SPK) operating via the Spark Agent in the Sky Atlas (Sky ecosystem) (Spark Docs) Morpho Governance (MORPHO token); governance whitelists IRMs/LLTVs and can activate fee switch (docs.morpho.org)": "Reflexer protocol community + FLX (“ungovernance”) holders with a stated goal of governance minimization over time (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Oracle Dependencies Primarily Chainlink price feeds with protocol risk controls (market-config dependent) Chainlink price feeds (primary), with protocol-defined fallbacks/guards Decentralized Oracle Network (Maker Oracles) with Chainlink integrations and redundancy Oracle-driven risk system; Spark has integrated oracle providers (e.g., RedStone) for lending markets (RedStone blog) Oracle per market; Morpho established an oracle wrapper for Chainlink feeds to support initial markets (morpho.org)": "Oracle stack includes OracleRelayer + OSM feeding safety and liquidation prices into core system logic (price + redemption price adjustments) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Parameter Control Governance-gated risk parameters + emergency controls (typical DeFi risk-admin pattern) Governance-gated parameters; admin/guardian controls for emergencies (especially during upgrades) Fully governance-controlled parameters; emergency shutdown and circuit breakers exist Parameter updates controlled through governance actions on the Spark Agent (risk, budgets, onboarding, deployments) (Spark Docs) Governance whitelists key risk parameters (LLTVs, IRMs) and can toggle fee switch (capped) (docs.morpho.org)": "Governance minimization guide documents which modules can be “ungoverned” vs where governance remains (e.g., oracle-related components / saviours) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Practitioner Validation Check YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced by contracts (HF<1) (aave.com) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced by contracts • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced via protocol auctions • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation rules enforced (HF<1) (Spark Docs) • YES positions unwindable programmatically YES creates credit onchain • YES liquidation enforced (LTV>LLTV) (docs.morpho.org) • YES positions unwindable programmatically": "YES creates credit onchain (SAFE → mint RAI) (Reflexer) • YES liquidation enforced (LiquidationEngine → auctions) (docs.reflexer.finance) • YES unwindable programmatically (repay debt, withdraw collateral; liquidations auction collateral) (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Practitioner’s Note Research focus: liquidation mechanics (health factor dynamics), collateral mix concentration, oracle coverage/fallbacks, and governance latency during fast markets. Also track version/market fragmentation (v1 frozen vs v3 active) when analyzing risk. (messari.io) Research focus: differences between v2 and v3 risk profiles; base-asset concentration in v3; liquidation throughput under stress; governance response speed during incidents. Research focus: auction efficiency during stress, oracle latency, RWA exposure and offchain enforcement risk, governance concentration, and emergency shutdown assumptions. Watchpoints: Aave v3 fork deltas (custom DAI/sDAI logic), oracle stack and feed coverage, asset-list governance, and liquidation throughput under stablecoin stress. Also note Spark’s bug bounty posture. (Spark Docs) Watchpoints: oracle selection/config is a first-order risk surface (market-by-market). Validate LLTV choice, oracle robustness, and liquidation liquidity for collateral. Review post-mortems for oracle manipulation and operational incidents. (Morpho Governance Forum)": "Watchpoints: (1) keeper participation and auction efficiency under fast ETH moves, (2) oracle/relayer correctness (safety vs liquidation price paths), (3) redemption rate regime shifts (impact on leverage incentives), (4) governance-minimization stage and any remaining admin surfaces. (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Primary Role in DeFi Base credit + leverage layer for Ethereum DeFi Base credit layer and leverage primitive for Ethereum DeFi Stablecoin issuance + base credit layer for DeFi DAI-centered credit & liquidity venue; major stablecoin + ETH collateral borrowing/supply rails inside Sky ecosystem (Blockworks) Base lending primitive for permissionless risk markets; “lending infrastructure” others build vaults/allocators on top of": "Governance-minimized, ETH-backed stable-credit primitive (non-fiat-pegged “reflex index”) used as collateral and settlement asset in DeFi (Reflexer)", "Protocol Status Active (v3 widely used; v1 largely frozen) (messari.io) Active (v3 “Comet” is primary; v2 largely deprecated/frozen for growth) Active (DAI issuance core to Ethereum DeFi) Active Active": "Active (RAI system live; governance minimization roadmap documented) (Reflexer)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending; collateralized credit issuance; onchain interest rate mechanics; liquidation + solvency enforced by protocol logic. (aave.com) Meets criteria: issues credit onchain against collateral; defines interest rates, liquidation logic, and solvency rules fully in smart contracts. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing; collateralized credit issuance; explicit liquidation and solvency logic; interest (stability fees) set and enforced onchain. Meets criteria: onchain borrowing/lending, collateralized credit issuance, onchain interest + liquidation + solvency rules. (Spark Docs) Meets criteria: creates credit and enforces liquidation/solvency fully onchain; interest and risk logic are protocol-defined per market. (docs.morpho.org)": "Meets criteria: onchain borrowing, collateralized credit issuance (RAI), protocol-defined solvency + liquidation (LiquidationEngine + auctions), and onchain monetary policy (redemption rate/price). (docs.reflexer.finance)", "Systemic Risk Exposure High (systemically important liquidity + collateral hub) High (core, long-lived DeFi credit primitive with broad integrations) Very High (DAI is systemically embedded across DeFi and beyond) High (meaningful stablecoin and ETH market integration within Sky ecosystem) (Blockworks) High (rapidly becoming core lending primitive; systemic exposure rises with integration density)": "Medium (important conceptually; smaller systemic footprint than DAI/USDC rails, but can be critical in niche strategies) (CoinGecko)", "Upstream Dependencies DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; oracle networks; stablecoin liquidity; governance/risk stewards Oracles (Chainlink); DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; stablecoin liquidity Oracles; keeper/liquidation infrastructure; governance processes; real-world legal structures (for RWAs) Oracles; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution; Sky/Maker liquidity inputs; governance operations (Blockworks) Oracles; liquidator/keeper ecosystem; market curation/allocators; DEX liquidity for liquidation execution": "ETH liquidity; oracle reliability; keeper/auction participation; RAI secondary market liquidity (docs.reflexer.finance)"}, "source_label": "Lending Markets"}'::jsonb),
  ('sushiswap', 'SushiSwap', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://www.sushi.com', ARRAY['Pool-based swaps executed fully onchain']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A general-purpose AMM offering permissionless token swaps and liquidity provision, with broad asset coverage and strong long-tail liquidity.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Uniform liquidity (v2-style pools)", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Constant Product AMM (Uniswap v2-style)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "Medium LP concentration risk; Medium dependency on incentives for liquidity depth", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-controlled fee splits (LP vs protocol)", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO token governance (SUSHI)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Governance and treasury stress events (2021–2022); no core AMM insolvency events", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Yield strategies, DAO treasury swaps, long-tail asset liquidity", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2020", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Permissionless LPs", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "High (AMM MEV exposure similar to Uniswap v2)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Sushi DAO (governance) with Sushi core contributors maintaining protocol", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Prices used internally and by integrators; not a primary canonical oracle source", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM • YES non-custodial settlement", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Key diligence: protocol governance stability (post-2021 restructurings), sustainability of incentives, and depth of liquidity vs Uniswap on major pairs. Sushi often matters more for coverage than dominance.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Continuous onchain pricing via AMM invariant", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, long-tail ERC-20s", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Active (Ethereum deployment ongoing; multi-chain presence)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Meets criteria: owns execution logic, settles swaps onchain, and contributes to spot price discovery across many ERC-20 pairs.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "Medium–High (important secondary liquidity venue; not the primary price anchor)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('balancer', 'Balancer', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://balancer.fi', ARRAY['Vault-based onchain swaps across custom pools']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A programmable liquidity protocol enabling multi-asset and weighted pools, optimized for portfolio-style liquidity and capital-efficient baskets.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Weighted pools, boosted pools, composable pools", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Programmable / Weighted AMM", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "Medium–High concentration risk in specific pool types (LSTs, DAO-managed pools)", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-set pool fees; flexible per-pool configuration", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO token governance (BAL)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Generally resilient; stress expresses via pool rebalancing and fee volatility rather than protocol failure", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "LST liquidity, DAO treasury management, index-like exposure, lending collateral pricing", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2020", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Permissionless LPs; DAO-managed pools", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Medium (Vault + batch swaps reduce some MEV, but not eliminated)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Balancer DAO with Balancer Labs as core contributor", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Native prices used internally and externally (especially for LST baskets and treasury pricing)", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via pools • YES non-custodial settlement", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Key diligence: pool composition risk (multi-asset exposure), reliance on a smaller set of sophisticated LPs, and smart-contract surface area of the Vault architecture.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Continuous onchain pricing via generalized AMM math", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "ETH pairs, stablecoin baskets, LST baskets, multi-asset pools", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Active (v2 architecture dominant)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines pricing via AMM math, and provides critical price discovery for basketized assets.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "High (critical for LST baskets, DAO treasuries, and non-standard liquidity structures)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('curve-finance', 'Curve Finance', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://curve.fi', ARRAY['Pool-based swaps executed fully onchain']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A specialized AMM optimized for stable and correlated assets, providing deep liquidity and minimal slippage near target prices.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Highly capital-efficient stableswap invariants", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Stable / invariant-based AMM", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "High dependence on a few major stablecoins/LSTs; High reliance by downstream protocols", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-set fees and gauge emissions", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO token governance (CRV)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Proven through multiple depeg cycles (USDC 2023, others); stress shows as pool imbalance, not protocol failure", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Lending liquidations, stablecoin pegs, LST pricing, yield strategies", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2020", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Permissionless LPs; DAO-directed liquidity via gauges", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Medium (lower toxic MEV due to low volatility pairs; still arb-driven)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Curve DAO (CRV governance) with Curve core contributors", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Native prices heavily referenced for stablecoins and LSTs (de facto peg oracle)", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM • YES non-custodial settlement", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Key diligence: peg defense relies on LP depth and incentives; gauge politics affect liquidity placement; depeg events test pool resilience more than smart contracts.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Continuous onchain pricing optimized for low-slippage around peg", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "Stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, correlated assets (e.g., ETH/LST)", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Active (Ethereum mainnet core; multi-chain deployments)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines pricing via invariant math, and is a primary price discovery venue for stablecoins and LSTs.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "Very High (critical for stablecoin and LST pricing across Ethereum DeFi)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('maverick-protocol', 'Maverick Protocol', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://www.mav.xyz', ARRAY['Pool-based swaps with automatic liquidity movement']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A next-generation AMM where liquidity automatically shifts directionally with price, reducing LP management overhead and adverse selection.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Dynamic liquidity that repositions with price moves", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Dynamic / directional AMM", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "Medium LP sophistication concentration; adoption/liquidity depth risk", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-configurable fees and pool parameters", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO governance (MAV)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Limited long-cycle stress history; monitor behavior during sharp trend reversals", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Emerging integrations; used by sophisticated LPs seeking efficiency", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2023", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Permissionless LPs", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Medium (design aims to reduce LP adverse selection vs static AMMs)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Maverick DAO / Maverick team (protocol governance and development)", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Internal pricing only; not widely used as a canonical oracle", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM • YES non-custodial settlement", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Key diligence: understand directional modes and LP exposure profiles; liquidity can concentrate rapidly, changing depth characteristics during volatility.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Continuous onchain pricing with liquidity that follows price", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, volatile assets", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, owns pricing/execution logic, and contributes to spot price discovery for supported pairs.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "Medium (innovative design, but not a primary system price anchor yet)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('dydx-v3-on-ethereum', 'dYdX (v3 on Ethereum)', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://dydx.exchange', ARRAY['Onchain settlement with offchain order matching (v3 hybrid)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A hybrid DEX that historically executed and settled trades on Ethereum using an order book model, contributing to price discovery via matched trades.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Margin-efficient, order-book execution", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Order book–style perpetual DEX (spot execution context historically on Ethereum)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "High reliance on market makers; Medium oracle and ops dependency", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-set fees and parameters", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO governance (DYDX)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Operated through high-volatility periods without AMM-style LP failures; migration reflects scaling tradeoffs", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Reference architecture for hybrid onchain DEX design; historical integrations", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Professional market makers (permissioned in v3 era)", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Medium (hybrid design reduced some AMM MEV vectors)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "dYdX Trading Inc. with governance by dYdX DAO", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Uses external oracles for pricing/settlement checks", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executed trades settled on Ethereum (v3) • YES prices set via matched trades • YES non-custodial settlement at the protocol layer", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Context matters: include only the Ethereum v3 era. Useful as a reference for hybrid designs; exclude current app-chain operations when analyzing Ethereum-native liquidity today.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Order book price discovery anchored by onchain settlement", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "ETH and major ERC-20 pairs (perps context; spot execution historically present)", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Deprecated on Ethereum (migrated to app-chain later)", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Included for historical Ethereum DEX execution: owned execution logic, settled onchain, and contributed to price discovery during its Ethereum-native phase.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "Medium (historical)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('0x-protocol', '0x Protocol', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://0x.org', ARRAY['Onchain settlement of RFQ and limit orders']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A DEX protocol enabling onchain settlement of RFQ and limit orders, where prices are quoted by market makers and executed trustlessly on Ethereum.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Capital-efficient RFQ fills (no passive LP capital)", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "RFQ / Hybrid onchain execution protocol", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "High MM concentration risk; Medium dependency on integrators’ flow", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-controlled fees (varies by deployment)", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO governance (ZRX)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Resilient; stress shows as liquidity withdrawal by MMs rather than protocol failure", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Widely embedded in wallets, dApps, and institutional flows", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2017", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Professional market makers (RFQ)", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Low–Medium (RFQ reduces sandwich risk)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "0x DAO with development by 0x Labs", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Limited oracle dependence; prices set by quotes", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES settles trades onchain • YES prices set via quotes executed onchain • YES non-custodial settlement", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Scope carefully: include RFQ/onchain fills; exclude pure routing/aggregation use. Key value is MEV-resistant execution for large trades.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Quote-driven price discovery settled onchain", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "Major ERC-20 pairs; stablecoin pairs", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Included when used for onchain execution: it owns settlement logic and sets prices via onchain trades (RFQ fills), not merely routing.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "High (infrastructure-level importance; execution layer for many apps)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb),
  ('cow-protocol', 'Cow Protocol', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'dexs-liquidity-protocols', 'https://cow.fi', ARRAY['Batch auctions settled onchain via a settlement contract', 'solver competition']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "A DEX that batches trades and clears them at a uniform price, leveraging solver competition to minimize MEV and improve execution.", "extras": {"Capital Efficiency Design Concentrated liquidity ranges (v3); uniform liquidity (v2)": "Capital-efficient via netting and coincidence-of-wants", "DEX Model Concentrated Liquidity AMM (v3); Constant Product AMM (v2 legacy)": "Batch auction / RFQ hybrid", "Dependency Concentration Risk High reliance by downstream protocols; High LP concentration risk in key pools; High MEV exposure by design": "Medium solver concentration risk; Medium dependency on underlying AMM liquidity for fallback", "Fee Control Fee tiers are protocol-defined; fee switches and new parameters are governance-controlled (not all activated)": "Governance-set protocol fees", "Governance Model DAO token governance (UNI)": "DAO governance (COW)", "Historical Stress Behavior Proven resilience through volatility events (2020–2024); stress typically expresses as fee spikes and LP reallocation, not protocol failure": "Resilient during volatility; stress shows as higher reliance on AMM fallback rather than failed settlement", "Integration Footprint Lending liquidations, yield strategies, derivatives pricing, oracle references, treasury swaps": "Wallet integrations, DAO treasury trades, institutional-sized swaps", "Launch Year 2018 (v1); v2 2020; v3 2021": "2021", "Liquidity Providers Permissionless LPs": "Professional solvers + AMM liquidity as fallback", "MEV Exposure Profile High (classic AMM MEV exposure: sandwiching, arbitrage)": "Low (designed to minimize MEV via batch auctions)", "Maintaining Organization Uniswap DAO (governance) with development by Uniswap Labs": "Cow DAO (Gnosis ecosystem)", "Oracle Usage Native price output widely used externally (TWAPs referenced by oracles, lending, and derivatives)": "Limited oracle dependence; prices emerge from auction clearing", "Practitioner Validation Check YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via AMM curves • YES non-custodial settlement": "YES executes trades onchain • YES sets prices via batch clearing • YES non-custodial settlement", "Practitioner’s Note Key diligence: LP risk is non-trivial in v3 (range management, active rebalancing). Watch MEV exposure, LP concentration in narrow ranges, and dependency risk where Uniswap TWAPs act as de facto oracles.": "Key diligence: solver set health and competition, fallback reliance on AMMs during thin auctions, and latency tradeoffs vs continuous AMMs.", "Price Discovery Method Continuous onchain pricing via AMM curves": "Uniform clearing price per batch (auction-based price discovery)", "Primary Trading Pairs ETH pairs, stablecoin pairs, LST pairs, long-tail ERC-20s": "Major ERC-20s; stablecoin pairs; ETH pairs", "Protocol Status Active (v3 dominant on Ethereum)": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion Meets criteria: executes swaps onchain, defines its own pricing mechanism, and is a primary source of spot price discovery on Ethereum.": "Meets criteria: owns execution logic, settles trades onchain, and sets prices through auction clearing on Ethereum.", "Systemic Importance Very High (arguably the most systemically important spot DEX on Ethereum)": "High (critical MEV-resistant execution layer for large trades)"}, "source_label": "DEXs & Liquidity Protocols"}'::jsonb)
) AS v(slug, name, sector_slug, subsector_slug, website, chains, tags, meta)
JOIN public.sectors sec ON sec.slug = v.sector_slug
JOIN public.subsectors s ON s.sector_id = sec.id AND s.slug = v.subsector_slug
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  name = EXCLUDED.name,
  subsector_id = EXCLUDED.subsector_id,
  website = EXCLUDED.website,
  chains = EXCLUDED.chains,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags,
  meta = EXCLUDED.meta,
  updated_at = NOW();

