3). (docs.yearn.fi) Diligence checklist: (1) strategy contract risk (each vault is a different strategy), (2) reward token swap-path slippage/MEV, (3) upstream protocol risk (Curve/Convex/DEX LPs), (4) chain-bridge considerations if allocating cross-chain, (5) TVL concentration by a few flagship vaults. (docs.beefy.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) per-vault strategy complexity, (2) reliance on Curve/LP mechanics (historically relevant), (3) upgrade/timelock and admin controls, (4) withdrawal assumptions under stress, (5) post-incident security posture and audits. (Least Authority) Diligence checklist: (1) maturity and implied rate curve behavior, (2) oracle/market pricing assumptions for PT/YT, (3) liquidity depth around maturity, (4) underlying yield source risk (what generates the yield), (5) incentive/governance concentration risk. (docs.pendle.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) maturity/term risk, (2) PT discount mechanics (fixed rate only if PT bought at discount), (3) liquidity depth in PT markets, (4) underlying yield asset assumptions. (Delv Documentation) Boundary caution: Notional sits near Lending Markets. Classify here when your analysis is about rate curve / maturity markets (fCash) and yield transformation; classify in Lending when focusing on credit creation and collateral rules. (docs.notional.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) strategy payoff under spot/vol regime shifts, (2) vault parameter/upgrade controls, (3) settlement/oracle upgrade risk, (4) liquidity/withdrawal mechanics by epoch, (5) tail-risk events (vault drains / contract issues). (theblock.co) Risk flags dominate: (1) regulatory enforcement precedent (SEC), (2) governance/ops centralization risk, (3) underlying venue concentration, (4) product run-off / deprecation risk, (5) liquidity/exit constraints for bond-like products. (lexology.com) Diligence checklist: (1) what the tranche’s underlying strategy venue is, (2) coverage mechanics (how junior absorbs losses), (3) concentration in a single underlying market, (4) oracle/venue liquidation behavior, (5) governance/upgrade controls. (docs.idle.finance)": "Boundary: Enzyme is a framework. Classify here only if the fund’s mandate is yield engineering; otherwise classify under asset management tooling.", "Principal Protection None (no guaranteed principal protection; depends on upstream protocols) None None None (no guaranteed principal protection; PT value depends on underlying + market discount) None (economic “fixed rate” comes from PT discount; no guarantee beyond underlying solvency) (Delv Documentation) None (protocol enforces redemption mechanics; principal depends on protocol solvency/market + collateral rules) None (strategy risk is explicit; drawdowns possible) (openzeppelin.com) Not guaranteed; product framing implies structured payoffs but depends on underlying + pool rules Conditional (Senior has built-in protection via Junior counterparty, within tranche design limits) (docs.idle.finance)": "None", "Protocol Status Active (Vaults, including V3 allocator vault architecture) (docs.yearn.fi) Active (multi-chain; Ethereum-supported vaults) (docs.beefy.finance) Active (vault/strategy architecture documented; Ethereum focus in docs) (Harvest Finance) Active Historical / reduced activity (kept for design relevance: PT/YT fixed-income design) (Delv Documentation) Active (focus here: fixed-rate yield structuring via fCash) (docs.notional.finance) Legacy structured vaults exist; operational context changed (rebrand + legacy vault incident Dec 2025) (theblock.co) Constrained / high regulatory risk (SEC settlement Dec 2023 on SMART Yield) (lexology.com) Active": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion Fits criteria: abstracts/aggregates yield, programmatically manages strategies across multiple protocols, transforms exposure via vault strategy logic (not a single primitive). (Medium) Fits criteria: abstracts yield, programmatically manages strategies across multiple protocols, and transforms exposure via automated compounding/position management. (docs.beefy.finance) Fits criteria: programmatic strategy logic deploying capital across multiple protocols; transformed yield exposure via autocompounding and strategy routing. (Harvest Finance) Fits criteria: transforms yield exposure (fixed/variable) and depends on multi-protocol yield sources + programmatic tokenization/market logic. (docs.pendle.finance) Fits criteria: transformed yield exposure via PT/YT engineering and multi-protocol yield inputs; included explicitly as historical/design-relevant. (Delv Documentation) Included only for the yield-structuring component: it transforms yield into a term structure (fixed-rate markets) rather than simply sourcing yield from one primitive. (docs.notional.finance) Fits criteria: yield is engineered and transformed via strategy logic (options-selling) rather than sourced from a single primitive. (docs.ribbon.finance) Fits criteria: yield depends on multi-protocol aggregation and structured payoff logic, not a single primitive. (CoinGecko) Fits criteria: abstracts yield across protocols and transforms exposure via tranching (risk-adjusted yield products). (docs.idle.finance)": "Included when used for yield strategies: yield is engineered via manager-driven, multi-protocol allocation, not a single primitive.", "Rebalancing Logic Strategy-defined (periodic + event-driven; allocator discretion in V3) (docs.yearn.fi) Event-driven/periodic compounding via harvest() workflows in strategies (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy-defined harvesting/compounding cycles (periodic + event-driven) (Harvest Finance) Market-driven; maturity-based lifecycle (PT/YT converge to maturity; AMM liquidity + solver/LP behavior) (docs.pendle.finance) Maturity-driven; PT redemption at term, YT captures differential yield (Delv Documentation) Maturity-based: fCash redeems at face value at maturity; trading implies fixed rate (docs.notional.finance) Periodic (weekly options cycles) (docs.ribbon.finance) Term-/pool-structure driven (bond-like) Periodic / event-driven (strategy-dependent)": "Manager-initiated; policy-constrained", "Risk Transformation Optimization + risk-adjusted routing (yield abstraction; not classic tranching by default) (Medium) Optimization (autocompounding + routing to underlying farms/LPs) (docs.beefy.finance) Optimization (routes to underlying protocols + compounds) (Harvest Finance) Duration + yield separation (turns yield into a tradable component; enables fixed-rate via PT discounting) (docs.pendle.finance) Duration transformation + yield separation (zero-coupon style via discounted PT) (Delv Documentation) Duration transformation (creates fixed-term claims, fCash) (docs.notional.finance) Volatility → yield transformation (systematically converts vol risk into premium capture) (docs.ribbon.finance) Risk tranching / structured finance (bonds/pools segment exposure) (lexology.com) Risk transformation (Senior/Junior tranches): senior gets protection, junior takes first loss for boosted yield (docs.idle.finance)": "Depends on mandate (can include risk limits, diversification rules)", "Strategy Change Control Governance-/manager-approved strategy onboarding and parameterization (allocator vault “plug & play” with manager choice) (docs.yearn.fi) Strategy/vault additions are gated by protocol processes (strategy contracts define capital deployment logic) (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy changes are controlled via protocol mechanisms (vault↔strategy linkage and upgrade controls), strategy development guided in repo/docs (GitHub) Governance/ops controls which markets/assets are supported and how incentives are allocated Admin/governance selects supported assets/terms and contract deployments Governance controls risk params/markets and upgrades (per governance processes) Strategy params and vault operations are not “set-and-forget” immutable; validate admin/upgrade controls per deployment (openzeppelin.com) Strategy/product operation and ongoing maintenance were treated as operationally controlled (per enforcement narratives) (klgates.com) Strategy integrations guided by a documented risk framework; additions/changes are governance/ops-mediated (docs.idle.finance)": "Policy-gated: managers act within on-chain risk policies; upgrades via governance", "Strategy Management Mixed: strategy authors + vault managers; governance/ops oversight via Multi-DAO + multisig execution (docs.yearn.fi) Strategy contracts + DAO-approved strategy framework (practically: contributors maintain strategy library) (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy contracts (explicitly described as defining how vault funds are used in 3rd party protocols) (Harvest Finance) Programmatic yield tokenization + AMM markets; governance directs incentives/market support Programmatic tokenization + AMM markets for PT/YT Protocol-defined market structure (maturities, fCash issuance/redemption rules) (docs.notional.finance) Automated strategy vaults (rule-based; typically weekly cadence) (docs.ribbon.finance) Protocol-defined structuring (bonds/pools) with governance/ops historically involved (klgates.com) Algorithmic allocation + productized tranche mechanics; risk framework for integrating new markets (docs.idle.finance)": "Manager-curated vaults (on-chain asset management)", "Strategy Scope Multi-protocol (core design) Multi-protocol (per-vault strategies allocate into LPs/farms and reinvest rewards) (docs.beefy.finance) Multi-protocol (vault funds deployed into 3rd party protocols via strategies) (Harvest Finance) Multi-protocol (depends on integrated yield-bearing assets across DeFi) (docs.pendle.finance) Multi-protocol (depends on integrated yield assets) Primarily internal markets (Notional-native pools); upstream yield legs can include cToken-style yield for LPs (implementation-dependent) (Medium) Multi-protocol (vault logic + options infrastructure + settlement) Multi-protocol (aggregates yield from underlying venues and re-slices into structured tranches/bonds) (CoinGecko) Multi-protocol (allocates across integrated markets; tranche strategies point to underlying venues) (docs.idle.finance)": "Multi-protocol (funds can deploy across lending, DEXs, LSTs, derivatives)", "Underlying Yield Sources Lending (Aave/Compound), LP positions (Curve/Uni/Balancer), incentives, other DeFi yield legs (strategy-dependent) (Medium) LP fees (DEXs), lending yield (where used), incentive rewards (farm tokens), CLM where applicable (docs.beefy.finance) Lending yield, LP fees, incentive rewards (strategy-dependent) (Harvest Finance) Yield-bearing tokens (e.g., lending receipts, LSTs, incentive-bearing wrappers), rewards streams (asset-dependent) (docs.pendle.finance) Yield-bearing assets (lending receipts, LP-like yield assets depending on supported integrations) Fixed-rate lending/borrowing; LP yield from pool fees + underlying interest sources (nToken context) (Medium) Options premium (systematic selling), sometimes paired with lending/treasury products (product-dependent) (docs.ribbon.finance) Aggregated yield from “different protocols” per overviews of SMART Yield concept (CoinGecko) Lending markets / strategy venues integrated into Best Yield + Tranches (per-asset strategy) (docs.idle.finance)": "Lending interest, LP fees, incentives, structured products (manager-selected)", "Upstream Dependencies Lending markets, DEXs/LP venues, oracles (indirect), keeper networks, bridges/LP gauges (strategy-dependent) (Medium) DEXs (Uniswap/Curve/etc.), farm platforms (Convex-style), token swap liquidity for compounding, chain-specific infra (docs.beefy.finance) 3rd party protocols (Curve/lending/DEXs), price/liquidity conditions for safe unwinds, keeper/executor processes (Harvest Finance) Tokenization contracts (SY/PT/YT), AMM liquidity engines, underlying protocols that generate yield (lending, staking/LSTs, etc.) (docs.pendle.finance) Tokenization contracts, AMM liquidity, underlying yield sources Native liquidity pools, collateral valuation + risk module