.finance) Term-/pool-structure driven (bond-like) Periodic / event-driven (strategy-dependent)": "Event-driven + periodic (allocation across yield legs)", "Risk Transformation Optimization + risk-adjusted routing (yield abstraction; not classic tranching by default) (Medium) Optimization (autocompounding + routing to underlying farms/LPs) (docs.beefy.finance) Optimization (routes to underlying protocols + compounds) (Harvest Finance) Duration + yield separation (turns yield into a tradable component; enables fixed-rate via PT discounting) (docs.pendle.finance) Duration transformation + yield separation (zero-coupon style via discounted PT) (Delv Documentation) Duration transformation (creates fixed-term claims, fCash) (docs.notional.finance) Volatility → yield transformation (systematically converts vol risk into premium capture) (docs.ribbon.finance) Risk tranching / structured finance (bonds/pools segment exposure) (lexology.com) Risk transformation (Senior/Junior tranches): senior gets protection, junior takes first loss for boosted yield (docs.idle.finance)": "Yield stacking + abstraction (packages multiple yield sources into a single cash-like product)", "Strategy Change Control Governance-/manager-approved strategy onboarding and parameterization (allocator vault “plug & play” with manager choice) (docs.yearn.fi) Strategy/vault additions are gated by protocol processes (strategy contracts define capital deployment logic) (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy changes are controlled via protocol mechanisms (vault↔strategy linkage and upgrade controls), strategy development guided in repo/docs (GitHub) Governance/ops controls which markets/assets are supported and how incentives are allocated Admin/governance selects supported assets/terms and contract deployments Governance controls risk params/markets and upgrades (per governance processes) Strategy params and vault operations are not “set-and-forget” immutable; validate admin/upgrade controls per deployment (openzeppelin.com) Strategy/product operation and ongoing maintenance were treated as operationally controlled (per enforcement narratives) (klgates.com) Strategy integrations guided by a documented risk framework; additions/changes are governance/ops-mediated (docs.idle.finance)": "Strategy parameters managed at product level; upgrades via governance/ops", "Strategy Management Mixed: strategy authors + vault managers; governance/ops oversight via Multi-DAO + multisig execution (docs.yearn.fi) Strategy contracts + DAO-approved strategy framework (practically: contributors maintain strategy library) (docs.beefy.finance) Strategy contracts (explicitly described as defining how vault funds are used in 3rd party protocols) (Harvest Finance) Programmatic yield tokenization + AMM markets; governance directs incentives/market support Programmatic tokenization + AMM markets for PT/YT Protocol-defined market structure (maturities, fCash issuance/redemption rules) (docs.notional.finance) Automated strategy vaults (rule-based; typically weekly cadence) (docs.ribbon.finance) Protocol-defined structuring (bonds/pools) with governance/ops historically involved (klgates.com) Algorithmic allocation + productized tranche mechanics; risk framework for integrating new markets (docs.idle.finance)": "Product-defined strategy logic (protocol-managed)", "Strategy Scope Multi-protocol (core design) Multi-protocol (per-vault strategies allocate into LPs/farms and reinvest rewards) (docs.beefy.finance) Multi-protocol (vault funds deployed into 3rd party protocols via strategies) (Harvest Finance) Multi-protocol (depends on integrated yield-bearing assets across DeFi) (docs.pendle.finance) Multi-protocol (depends on integrated yield assets) Primarily internal markets (Notional-native pools); upstream yield legs can include cToken-style yield for LPs (implementation-dependent) (Medium) Multi-protocol (vault logic + options infrastructure + settlement) Multi-protocol (aggregates yield from underlying venues and re-slices into structured tranches/bonds) (CoinGecko) Multi-protocol (allocates across integrated markets; tranche strategies point to underlying venues) (docs.idle.finance)": "Multi-protocol (restaking + DeFi routing)", "Underlying Yield Sources Lending (Aave/Compound), LP positions (Curve/Uni/Balancer), incentives, other DeFi yield legs (strategy-dependent) (Medium) LP fees (DEXs), lending yield (where used), incentive rewards (farm tokens), CLM where applicable (docs.beefy.finance) Lending yield, LP fees, incentive rewards (strategy-dependent) (Harvest Finance) Yield-bearing tokens (e.g., lending receipts, LSTs, incentive-bearing wrappers), rewards streams (asset-dependent) (docs.pendle.finance) Yield-bearing assets (lending receipts, LP-like yield assets depending on supported integrations) Fixed-rate lending/borrowing; LP yield from pool fees + underlying interest sources (nToken context) (Medium) Options premium (systematic selling), sometimes paired with lending/treasury products (product-dependent) (docs.ribbon.finance) Aggregated yield from “different protocols” per overviews of SMART Yield concept (CoinGecko) Lending markets / strategy venues integrated into Best Yield + Tranches (per-asset strategy) (docs.idle.finance)": "Restaking rewards (EigenLayer AVSs), base staking yield, DeFi yield legs (lending/LP where used)", "Upstream Dependencies Lending markets, DEXs/LP venues, oracles (indirect), keeper networks, bridges/LP gauges (strategy-dependent) (Medium) DEXs (Uniswap/Curve/etc.), farm platforms (Convex-style), token swap liquidity for compounding, chain-specific infra (docs.beefy.finance) 3rd party protocols (Curve/lending/DEXs), price/liquidity conditions for safe unwinds, keeper/executor processes (Harvest Finance) Tokenization contracts (SY/PT/YT), AMM liquidity engines, underlying protocols that generate yield (lending, staking/LSTs, etc.) (docs.pendle.finance) Tokenization contracts, AMM liquidity, underlying yield sources Native liquidity pools, collateral valuation + risk modules; oracle/valuation surfaces are a key diligence item (audit trail exists) (openzeppelin.com) Options infrastructure / vault contracts; relies on settlement correctness and any price/oracle upgrade surfaces relevant to vaults (theblock.co) Underlying yield venues; governance/ops controls; legal/compliance constraints now primary practical dependency (lexology.com) Underlying lending/strategy markets (e.g., Instadapp-based strategies in examples), oracles/keepers indirectly via venues (docs.idle.finance)": "LSTs / LRTs, restaking middleware (EigenLayer), DeFi venues used for cash-management legs", "Yield Model Aggregated + strategy vaults (optimized yield) Aggregated + autocompounding optimizer Aggregated yield vaults + autocompounding Structured / transformed yield (separates yield vs principal; enables fixed/variable exposure via PT/YT) (docs.pendle.finance) Structured yield (splits yield-bearing assets into Principal Tokens + Yield Tokens; fixed/variable via market pricing) (Delv Documentation) Fixed / term yield via fCash pricing in native liquidity pools (docs.notional.finance) Structured yield (options-selling “theta” style) Structured / tranched yield (SMART Yield) Aggregated + risk-tranching structured yield": "Structured / aggregated yield"}, "source_label": "Yield & Structured Markets"}'::jsonb)
) AS v(slug, name, sector_slug, subsector_slug, website, chains, tags, meta)
JOIN public.sectors sec ON sec.slug = v.sector_slug
JOIN public.subsectors s ON s.sector_id = sec.id AND s.slug = v.subsector_slug
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  name = EXCLUDED.name,
  subsector_id = EXCLUDED.subsector_id,
  website = EXCLUDED.website,
  chains = EXCLUDED.chains,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags,
  meta = EXCLUDED.meta,
  updated_at = NOW();

