FROM (VALUES
  ('swell-yield-vault-products', 'Swell (Yield Vault Products)', 'defi-systems-architecture', 'yield-structured-markets', 'https://www.swellnetwork.io', ARRAY['Medium (vault adoption dependent)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Yield vault products that deploy Swell’s staking assets into additional DeFi strategies to enhance returns beyond base staking.", "extras": {"Capital Lockups Typically none at vault level (withdrawal constraints can exist per strategy/asset conditions; check per vault) (yearn.fi) Typically none at vault level (vault-specific withdrawal mechanics apply; verify per vault) (docs.beefy.finance) Typically none at vault level; withdrawal liquidity depends on upstream positions (verify per vault/strategy) (Harvest Finance) Maturity / term-structure is intrinsic (PT/YT exist “up to maturity”) (docs.pendle.finance) Yes (fixed term) — principal locked to maturity for PT holders (Delv Documentation) Yes (fixed term/maturity) (docs.notional.finance) Often epoch-like cycles (weekly) rather than free-form “anytime” yield; check per vault/product (docs.ribbon.finance) Often term-like “bond” framing (SMART Yield bonds) (lexology.com) Typically none strict, but tranche structure can imply different risk classes and coverage mechanics; validate per tranche": "Vault-specific (some strategies imply liquidity assumptions)", "Dependency Concentration Risk High upstream dependency stacking (Aave/Curve/Uni etc.); Medium governance/multisig execution concentration; Medium strategy-manager concentration (docs.yearn.fi) High upstream dependency stacking (LP farms + swap liquidity) • Medium strategy-maintainer concentration • Medium vault-level TVL concentration (docs.beefy.finance) High upstream dependency stacking • High strategy/implementation risk (vault-by-vault) • Medium governance/admin concentration risk (Harvest Finance) High dependency on supported yield-bearing collateral ecosystems; Medium governance/incentive concentration; Medium liquidity fragmentation risk across maturities (docs.pendle.finance) Medium dependency on underlying yield assets; Medium liquidity concentration risk in limited PT markets (Delv Documentation) Medium maturity liquidity concentration; Medium governance/risk-module dependency; Medium collateral/oracle valuation dependency (openzeppelin.com) High dependency on correct upgrade/oracle/settlement surfaces; Medium dependency on options liquidity regimes (theblock.co) Very High regulatory risk concentration; High governance/ops concentration; Medium dependency on underlying venues (lexology.com) High dependency on specific integrated venues per tranche; Medium governance/upgrade concentration; Medium liquidity/exit assumptions per tranche (docs.idle.finance)": "Medium–High dependency on specific DeFi venues; Medium governance concentration", "Downstream Consumers Retail vault depositors, DAO treasuries, structured products using yTokens, integrators sourcing yield Retail depositors, DAOs/treasuries seeking autocompounded exposure, integrators embedding vault yield Retail vault users, yield allocators, integrators (where applicable) Yield traders, DAOs/treasuries locking yield, structured product builders, hedgers/speculators Fixed-rate buyers (PT), variable yield seekers (YT), structured product builders (Delv Documentation) Fixed-income users (lend/borrow), LPs in maturity pools (nTokens), structured product builders referencing onchain rate curve Retail structured-yield users; DAOs via “Ribbon Treasury” style products (where applicable) (docs.ribbon.finance) Structured product participants; yield buyers seeking bond-like exposure Treasuries/DAOs and integrators seeking risk-adjusted yield via a single integration (idle.finance)": "Users seeking enhanced yield on top of Swell LST exposure", "Governance Model DAO governance with Multi-DAO workstreams + governance multisig execution layer (docs.yearn.fi) DAO governance (BIFI) + operational processes for strategy deployment (beefy.com) FARM governance + operational controls; docs also reference timelocks/controlled upgrades for strategy links (implementation-dependent) (Harvest Finance) Governance-driven incentives + parameter control (protocol-level) Governance/ops (protocol era-specific) Governance token (NOTE) + protocol ops Governance history + operational control surface (vault implementations + upgrades) (openzeppelin.com) DAO governance historically DAO governance": "Governance + protocol ops", "Historical Stress Behavior Battle-tested; stress typically manifests as strategy-specific losses/pauses and rapid reallocations rather than “bank-run” insolvency (validate per vault) (docs.yearn.fi) Stress manifests as upstream protocol issues, reward token volatility, or strategy/vault pauses; protocol docs emphasize autonomous contracts once deployed (operational continuity) (docs.beefy.finance) Notable exploit Oct 26, 2020 (~$24M) followed by large TVL outflows (“bank run” dynamic) (Nasdaq) Stress typically expresses as (a) liquidity fragmentation across maturities and (b) repricing of implied yields, not “vault insolvency” (docs.pendle.finance) Stress primarily appears as liquidity/market adoption constraints rather than protocol-driven yield failures (validate per term/market) (Delv Documentation) Stress tends to show up as (a) liquidity fragmentation across maturities and (b) collateral/risk parameter sensitivity rather than “strategy blowups” (docs.notional.finance) Dec 2025: legacy Ribbon DOV vaults reportedly drained (~$2.7M) after an oracle/upgrade-related issue (incident context) (theblock.co) Dec 22, 2023 SEC settlement impacted protocol operations and highlights structured-product regulatory sensitivity (lexology.com) Stress tends to surface as underlying market losses or tranche imbalance rather than “vault blowups” (evaluate per tranche/venue) (docs.idle.finance)": "Stress likely manifests as DeFi-venue exposure rather than staking failures", "Launch Year 2020 (YFI fair launch July 2020; iEarn origins Feb 2020) (CoinGecko) 2020 (vaults live Oct 8, 2020; origin Sept 2020) (docs.beefy.finance) 2020 (active protocol period; major exploit Oct 26, 2020) (Nasdaq) 2021 (V1 mainnet in June 2021) (Binance) 2021 (Ethereum mainnet launch June 30, 2021) (DELV) 2020 (V1; V2 later) (The Defiant) 2021 (Theta Vault era) (openzeppelin.com) 2020–2021 era (SMART Yield bonds/pools) (CoinGecko) 2019–2020 era (protocol matured into tranche suite by 2021) (Medium)": "2023", "Leverage Usage Conditional (some strategies may use leverage; vault-specific) Conditional (strategy-dependent; commonly no explicit leverage, but can include leveraged legs depending on vault design—validate per vault) (docs.beefy.finance) Usually no explicit leverage; strategy-dependent (validate per strategy) (Harvest Finance) Can be enabled at product level (leverage and structured positioning common via integrations; validate per market/product) Not inherent; depends on integrations Can be used implicitly via borrowing/lending; leverage exists at user level (collateralized borrowing) Not inherent; users can lever externally (protocol itself primarily structures strategy exposure) Not inherent Generally no protocol-native leverage; users can lever externally": "Not inherent", "Maintaining Organization Yearn “Multi-DAO” structure: YFI holders + yTeams + Governance Multisig (execution / veto) (docs.yearn.fi) Beefy DAO (BIFI governance) + community contributors; vaults/strategies documented as autonomous smart contracts once deployed (docs.beefy.finance) Harvest contributors + FARM governance; strategy development guidance published in repo/docs (GitHub) Pendle contributors + governance (ve-style mechanics exist in protocol design; ops via core contributors) Delv / Element contributors (protocol + docs maintained by Delv) (Delv Documentation) Notional contributors + governance (NOTE; protocol ops) (Notional Finance) Ribbon / Aevo team + token governance history (structured vault system documented) (openzeppelin.com) BarnBridge DAO + founders/ops historically (structured product pools) (lexology.com) Idle DAO + contributors (product suite: Best Yield + Yield Tranches) (docs.idle.finance)": "Swell team + governance", "Practitioner Validation Check YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation • YES yield transformed vs pass-through wrapper (Medium) YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation/compounding • YES transformed yield vs passive wrapper (docs.beefy.finance) YES multi-protocol strategy logic • YES programmatic allocation • YES yield transformed vs passive wrapper (Harvest Finance) YES multi-protocol yield inputs • YES programmatic transformation (PT/YT) • YES transformed exposure (fixed/variable, duration) (docs.pendle.finance) YES multi-protocol yield inputs • YES programmatic transformation (PT/YT) • YES fixed/variable exposures emerge from market structure (Delv Documentation) YES fixed/term transformation • YES programmatic market structure • PARTIAL multi-protocol dependency (more internal than Yearn/Pendle; still transforms yield) (docs.notional.finance) YES strategy transforms yield (premium capture) (docs.ribbon.finance) • YES automated program logic (openzeppelin.com) • YES not passive wrapper YES structured yield product using multi-protocol yield inputs (CoinGecko) • YES transforms exposure into bond/tranche form (lexology.com) YES multi-protocol strategy logic (docs.idle.finance) • YES programmatic allocation (GitHub) • YES transformed yield (tranches) (docs.idle.finance)": "YES multi-protocol • YES programmatic strategy • YES yield transformed vs base staking", "Practitioner’s Note Diligence checklist: (1) which upstream protocols the vault touches, (2) strategy upgrade/admin controls, (3) keeper dependencies, (4) withdrawal liquidity assumptions under stress, (5) smart-contract/audit coverage per vault version (v2 vs v3). (docs.yearn.fi) Diligence checklist: (1) strategy contract risk (each vault is a different strategy), (2) reward token swap-path slippage/MEV, (3) upstream protocol risk (Curve/Convex/DEX LPs), (4) chain-bridge considerations if allocating cross-chain, (5) TVL concentration by a few flagship vaults. (docs.beefy.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) per-vault strategy complexity, (2) reliance on Curve/LP mechanics (historically relevant), (3) upgrade/timelock and admin controls, (4) withdrawal assumptions under stress, (5) post-incident security posture and audits. (Least Authority) Diligence checklist: (1) maturity and implied rate curve behavior, (2) oracle/market pricing assumptions for PT/YT, (3) liquidity depth around maturity, (4) underlying yield source risk (what generates the yield), (5) incentive/governance concentration risk. (docs.pendle.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) maturity/term risk, (2) PT discount mechanics (fixed rate only if PT bought at discount), (3) liquidity depth in PT markets, (4) underlying yield asset assumptions. (Delv Documentation) Boundary caution: Notional sits near Lending Markets. Classify here when your analysis is about rate curve / maturity markets (fCash) and yield transformation; classify in Lending when focusing on credit creation and collateral rules. (docs.notional.finance) Diligence checklist: (1) strategy payoff under spot/vol regime shifts, (2) vault parameter/upgrade controls, (3) settlement/oracle upgrade risk, (4) liquidity/withdrawal mechanics by epoch, (5) tail-risk events (vault drains / contract issues). (theblock.co) Risk flags dominate: (1) regulatory enforcement precedent (SEC), (2) governance/ops centralization risk, (3) underlying venue concentration, (4) product run-off / deprecation risk, (5) liquidity/exit constraints for bond-like products. (lexology.com) Diligence checklist: (1) what the tranche’s underlying strategy venue is, (2) coverage mechanics (how junior absorbs losses), (3) concentration in a single underlying market, (4) oracle/venue liquidation behavior, (5) governance/upgrade controls. (docs.idle.finance)": "Boundary clarity: Swell LST belongs in the LST subsector. Only classify here when analyzing vault-level yield engineering.", "Principal Protection None (no guaranteed principal protection; depends on upstream protocols) None None None (no guaranteed principal protection; PT value depends on underlying + market discount) None (economic “fixed rate” comes from PT discount; no guarantee beyond underlying solvency) (Delv Documentation) None (protocol enforces redemption mechanics; principal depends on protocol solvency/market + collateral rules) None (strategy risk is explicit; drawdowns possible) (openzeppelin.com) Not guaranteed; product framing implies structured payoffs but depends on underlying + pool rules Conditional (Senior has built-in protection via Junior counterparty, within tranche design limits) (docs.idle.finance)": "None", "Protocol Status Active (Vaults, including V3 allocator vault architecture) (docs.yearn.fi) Active (multi-chain; Ethereum-supported vaults) (docs.beefy.finance) Active (vault/strategy architecture documented; Ethereum focus in docs) (Harvest Finance) Active Historical / reduced activity (kept for design relevance: PT/YT fixed-income design) (Delv Documentation) Active (focus here: fixed-rate yield structuring via fCash) (docs.notional.finance) Legacy structured vaults exist; operational context changed (rebrand + legacy vault incident Dec 2025) (theblock.co) Constrained / high regulatory risk (SEC settlement Dec 2023 on SMART Yield) (lexology.com) Active": "Active", "Reason for Inclusion Fits criteria: abstracts/aggregates yield, programmatically manages strategies across multiple protocols, transforms exposure via vault strategy logic (not a single primitive). (Medium) Fits criteria: abstracts yield, programmatically manages strategies across multiple protocols, and transforms exposure via automated compounding/position management. (docs.beefy.finance) Fits criteria: programmatic strategy logic deploy